@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="mb-4">
    <h1 class="h3 fw-bold mb-1">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-secondary small">Last updated: November 2026</p>
</div>

<div class="panel-card">
    <div class="panel-body">
        <h5 class="fw-bold mb-2">1. Scope and Purpose</h5>
        <p class="small text-secondary mb-3">
            This Privacy Policy describes how the EcoSanitize Municipal Operations Portal collects, handles, and stores operational information in connection with waste collection requests, facility sanitization audits, and related public sanitation services.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mb-2">2. Information We Collect</h5>
        <p class="small text-secondary mb-2">
            The system records only operational information required to carry out waste management and sanitation functions:
        </p>
        <ul class="small text-secondary mb-3">
            <li><strong>Location Data:</strong> Ward name, street address, or facility identifier provided for collection.</li>
            <li><strong>Waste Attributes:</strong> Segregation stream category, estimated weight, priority level, and special handling instructions.</li>
            <li><strong>Audit Logs:</strong> Facility name, cleanliness score, chemical disinfectant applied, inspection date, and inspector name.</li>
        </ul>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mb-2">3. Use of Information</h5>
        <p class="small text-secondary mb-2">
            Collected data is strictly used for:
        </p>
        <ul class="small text-secondary mb-3">
            <li>Dispatching municipal collection vehicles and assigning field drivers.</li>
            <li>Ensuring hazardous and sanitary materials are routed to authorized facilities.</li>
            <li>Scheduling re-inspection and deep cleaning for facilities that fail hygiene standards.</li>
            <li>Compiling municipal waste volume and compliance statistics.</li>
        </ul>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mb-2">4. Data Storage and Security</h5>
        <p class="small text-secondary mb-3">
            Operational records are stored securely within municipal application databases. Access is limited to authorized public health inspectors, dispatch coordinators, and facility administrators.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mb-2">5. Contact Information</h5>
        <p class="small text-secondary mb-0">
            For questions regarding this policy or data retained by this system, contact the Municipal Sanitation and Public Health Directorate through official municipal communication channels.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
